.TH KILIX-JPAK 6 "July 2026" "kilix-jpak 0.1.0" "Games"
.SH NAME
kilix-jpak \- clean-room Kitty-protocol starvault action game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kilix-jpak
.RI [ --level " N" ]
.br
.B kilix-jpak
.RI --selftest " [seed] [ticks]"
.br
.B kilix-jpak
.RI { --rules-test | --input-test | --render-test " [seed]" | --sound-test | --dump-campaign }
.br
.B kilix-jpak
.BI --dump-level " N"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Kilix JPAK: Deep Salvage
is a native terminal action-puzzle game with a 100-level campaign. Recover
every star mote, manage the micro-thruster, phase through quantum foam, operate
shape-coded gates and shutters, avoid eight machine families, and enter the
open starvault iris.
.PP
Vault pressure grows from one safely placed machine in the opening level to
as many as fifteen in the deepest chambers. Machines activate locally with a
visible, nonlethal warning tell instead of converging from the whole vault.
.PP
The title continues from the highest unlocked vault. Empty thruster fuel
slowly recovers to an eighteen-percent emergency reserve while Kilix is safely
grounded or on a rail. Retry attempts roll back unbanked score while preserving
elapsed vault time.
.PP
The campaign derives 100 unique structural signatures from ten named macro
families and uses more than 30 entry-to-iris routes. Chapter mutation changes
the macro layouts, while mandatory phase, shutter, and ring-gate side vaults
make featured mechanics meaningful. Reservation-aware generation protects
route anchors, required cells, objectives, and safe paths before placing
hazards and machines.
.PP
The game renders a code-native RGBA scene through the Kitty graphics protocol.
Each chapter has its own procedural background motif. The level selector uses
a layered semantic mini-map with entry and iris direction, pressure pips, and
present-system tags. The game has no external asset files and no dependency on
an original game installation.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B Left, A / Right, D
Walk.
.TP
.B Up, W / Down, S
Climb or descend magnetic rails.
.TP
.B Space, Z
Fire the fuel-limited micro-thruster.
.TP
.B X, E
Erode adjacent phase foam.
.TP
.B P, Escape
Pause or resume.
.TP
.B R
Spend one life and restart the current vault.
.TP
.B M
Toggle sound.
.TP
.B H
Open or close the field manual.
.TP
.B Q
Back or return to the title from pause.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --level " N"
Start level 1 through 100 in practice mode. Practice does not change campaign
unlocks or high score.
.TP
.BI --selftest " [seed] [ticks]"
Run deterministic headless simulation and every campaign level.
.TP
.B --rules-test
Run focused mechanics and campaign validation fixtures.
.TP
.B --input-test
Test held-key and press-only input paths.
.TP
.BI --render-test " [seed]"
Write twenty-two deterministic PPM scenes, including macro-family, mandatory
mechanic, chapter-variant, walking-stride, selector, and state fixtures.
.TP
.B --sound-test
Play every generated sound, or validate silent fallback.
.TP
.B --dump-campaign
Print the exact 100-row generated campaign manifest.
.TP
.BI --dump-level " N"
Print level 1 through 100 as an annotated semantic grid with entry, iris,
objectives, rails, hazards, and featured systems.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KILIX_JPAK_DATA_HOME
Override the parent directory used for the versioned profile.
.TP
.B KILIX_JPAK_RENDER_DIR
Output directory for render-test images.
.TP
.B KILIX_JPAK_SKIP_PROBE
Skip the Kitty graphics capability probe for controlled integration tests.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/kilix-jpak/profile.v1
Versioned high score, highest unlocked level, and sound preference.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kitty (1)
